          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Peter Jefferson and the Frontier Father",
          "content": "Thomas's father Peter Jefferson was a self-made surveyor, planter, and militia colonel. He helped map the Virginia-North Carolina border and amassed thousands of acres in the Piedmont. Peter died in 1757 when Thomas was 14, leaving him roughly 5,000 acres, dozens of enslaved people, and a sense of obligation to acquire learning beyond the frontier.",
