          "title": "William and Mary College 1760-1762",
          "content": "At 16 Jefferson rode to Williamsburg to enroll at the College of William and Mary, the second oldest college in British America. He spent two years there, mastering mathematics, Newtonian physics, and moral philosophy under Dr. William Small, a Scottish Enlightenment professor who became his intellectual father. Small introduced Jefferson to George Wythe and Governor Francis Fauquier.",
